From 801c35d130c595b9dc59318fc96293e6949a2791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 272/274] usb: typec: tcpm: Take Not_Supported as a VDM reply
 only once the VDM is sent

A Not_Supported Message received in SRC_READY or SNK_READY while the VDM
state machine is active ends the VDM AMS, on the assumption that it is
the port partner's reply to our VDM. That is only true once the VDM has
been transmitted and tcpm waits for the response (VDM_STATE_BUSY). As a
PD 3.x Source, tcpm first sets SinkTxNG and holds the VDM for tSinkTx in
VDM_STATE_SEND_MESSAGE; after a BUSY response it waits in
VDM_STATE_WAIT_RSP_BUSY. A Not_Supported that arrives in those states
answers some earlier Message of ours, and taking it as the reply drops a
VDM that was never sent.

When the dropped VDM is part of discovery, discovery stops for good:
nothing queues the next discovery step, so no alternate mode is ever
registered. This is seen with a USB-C DP/USB3 dongle, which answers
a Not_Supported from tcpm with a Not_Supported of its own just after
tcpm resumed discovery with Discover SVIDs:

  AMS DISCOVER_SVIDS start
  PD RX, header: 0x690 [1]        <- Not_Supported, during tSinkTx
  AMS DISCOVER_SVIDS finished     <- Discover SVIDs never sent
  (end of discovery)

Only take the Message as the reply in VDM_STATE_BUSY. If the VDM is still
to be sent, ignore the Message and let the VDM go out.

Fixes: f1fbd950b59b ("usb: typec: tcpm: Fix wrong handling for Not_Supported in VDM AMS")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
index 06c4ea34f..b8eebcb7c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -3891,13 +3891,24 @@ static void tcpm_pd_ctrl_request(struct tcpm_port *port,
 			break;
 		case SRC_READY:
 		case SNK_READY:
-			if (port->vdm_state > VDM_STATE_READY) {
+			/* The reply to the VDM that is waiting for a response */
+			if (port->vdm_state == VDM_STATE_BUSY) {
 				port->vdm_state = VDM_STATE_DONE;
 				if (tcpm_vdm_ams(port))
 					tcpm_ams_finish(port);
 				mod_vdm_delayed_work(port, 0);
 				break;
 			}
+			/*
+			 * The VDM is still to be sent, after tSinkTx or after
+			 * the partner answered BUSY, so this Message is not a
+			 * reply to it. Send the VDM as planned.
+			 */
+			if (port->vdm_state > VDM_STATE_READY) {
+				tcpm_log(port, "Ignoring ctrl msg %d, VDM not sent yet",
+					 type);
+				break;
+			}
 			fallthrough;
 		default:
 			tcpm_pd_handle_state(port,
